flat-1 = carries a closure, that is, a pointer outward
flat-2 = is recursive, and the size of a value is unbounded
flat-3 = is owned (§3.3), and such a value lives on the heap
flat-4 = is declared without a representation: there is no body or it is sealed; the dictionary of a sealed type is taken as a value - a member of its signature of the form `flat : Flat T` (§4.11)
